 by reading test pain signals — advisory only, no code changes. Use when tests are painful to write or maintain.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.agents/skills/test-friction/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>ui-align</name>\n    <description>High-alignment UI specification workflow using interactive grilling and methodology verification. Use when specifying UI through interactive grilling.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.agents/skills/ui-align/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>whisper</name>\n    <description>Deterministic knowledge workspace: session loop (recall all / append), scope routing, distill, bundle. Delegates to the turu CLI when installed; manual fallbacks otherwise.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.agents/skills/whisper/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>wrap-up</name>\n    <description>End-of-day review across all projects. Synthesizes work-queue entries into the log, flags undocumented work. Trigger when the user says /wrap-up, &apos;end of day&apos;, &apos;day review&apos;, or &apos;daily close&apos;.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.agents/skills/wrap-up/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>fck</name>\n    <description>Finish the sentence the user didn&apos;t write. Trigger when the user&apos;s message is primarily a swear — &quot;fuck&quot;, &quot;shit&quot;, &quot;oh shit&quot;, &quot;oh fuck&quot;, &quot;wtf&quot;, or elongated variants like &quot;fuuuuuk&quot; — instead of a description of a problem. Also for the explicit /fuck, /shit, /oh-shit, /oh-fuck, /fuuuuuk commands. The swear carries no content; the content is in what just happened on screen. Go look — last command, last edit, last error — and hand back a concrete diagnosis or the specific missing sentence, instead of asking &quot;what&apos;s wrong?&quot;, mirroring emotion, or lecturing about message quality. Extra repeated letters = more urgency (&quot;fuuuuuk&quot; vs &quot;fuck&quot;).</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.pi/agent/git/github.com/charly-vibes/fck/skills/fck/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>for-fucks-sake</name>\n    <description>Interview fallback when there is genuinely nothing in context to explain the user&apos;s frustration — no error, no recent edit, no obvious cause for a &quot;fuck&quot;/&quot;shit&quot;/&quot;wtf&quot;. Instead of guessing or asking an open-ended &quot;what&apos;s wrong?&quot;, ask exactly one question at a time, each with a best-guess answer attached so the user can confirm in one word. Also invoked directly as /for-fucks-sake.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.pi/agent/git/github.com/charly-vibes/fck/skills/for-fucks-sake/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>no-shit</name>\n    <description>Verification pass before calling any fix &quot;done&quot; — especially incident-tier fixes (/oh-shit, /oh-fuck, intensity 4-5). Check real output instead of trusting that the change was made, scan once for side effects, then state the verdict plainly. Use after applying any fix whose failure would matter, or when invoked directly as /no-shit. Replaces the one-shot &quot;fixed it&quot; claim with actual confirmation, stopping the moment it&apos;s genuinely confirmed.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.pi/agent/git/github.com/charly-vibes/fck/skills/no-shit/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>would-you-please-fucking-stop</name>\n    <description>Circuit-breaker for when the agent itself is the problem — looping on the same failed fix, hedging, restating the same answer without new information, or producing repetition instead of progress. Named after Ursula K. Le Guin&apos;s essay &quot;Would You Please Fucking Stop?&quot;. Use when frustration is aimed at how the conversation is going rather than at the task. Forces a reset to actual current state and exactly one concrete next step. Also invoked directly as /would-you-please-fucking-stop.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.pi/agent/git/github.com/charly-vibes/fck/skills/would-you-please-fucking-stop/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n</available_skills>\n</skills>","cwd":"<cwd>\n/var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina\n</cwd>"},"timestamp":1792530152248,"toolsAdded":[{"name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Shell command to execute"},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}}},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"ah_check","description":"Validate spec-test correspondence for the espectacular setup in the project: checks every deployed spec scenario against its contract TOML and, with run_tests, executes the declared contract tests. Prefer this over running `ah check` via bash — it returns the structured JSON envelope. Exit code 1 means findings exist.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"changes":{"type":"string","description":"In-flight openspec change name to validate with (change overlay)"},"project":{"type":"string","description":"Project root directory (defaults to the session working directory)"},"run_tests":{"type":"boolean","description":"Also execute declared contract tests (slower; default false)"}}}},{"name":"ah_doctor","description":"Diagnose the espectacular setup in the project: config, version drift, specs/changes dirs, managed blocks, hooks, and framework recommendations. Read-only.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"project":{"type":"string","description":"Project root directory (defaults to the session working directory)"}}}},{"name":"ah_signals","description":"Emit dont drift signals from the espectacular setup in the project. Read-only.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"project":{"type":"string","description":"Project root directory (defaults to the session working directory)"}}}},{"name":"ah_explain","description":"Playbook guidance for an espectacular finding kind, suggested action, or topic (e.g. no-tests-declared, contract-stale, workflow, scenario-scoped-tests). Returns the full guidance text.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["topic"],"properties":{"topic":{"type":"string","description":"Finding kind, suggested action, or topic slug"},"project":{"type":"string","description":"Project root directory (defaults to the session working directory)"}}}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are the cross-family verifier subagent for ticket evallerina-e4x (add-ecosystem-doc-evals phase 3). You are READ-ONLY: inspect, run gates, and report — never edit, commit, close, or spawn.\n\nClaim to verify (implementor session evallerina-e4x-implement1):\n1. src/routing.rs: audit rows ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED / ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE route through existing propose() verbatim — fingerprint token evallerina:<scenario>:<fault-class>, cross-model threshold min(3,|registry|), no new routing semantics.\n2. upstream=true tools (bd, openspec) emit skipped/unmapped_upstream proposals, never filed — pinned by test.\n3. Fingerprint dedup pinned by test (same token twice → one proposal).\n4. CLI: doc-audit routes audit rows through the filing path, dry-run by default; filing only behind --file.\n5. Task 3.2 evidence: .wai/projects/evallerina/research/evallerina-e4x-dry-run-review.org + proposed-tickets-doc-audit-e4x.jsonl (dry-run smoke reviewed, no filing).\n6. Gates: cargo test TOTAL 137 passed 0 failed; just tier0 exit 0; openspec tasks 3.1–3.2 checked in openspec/changes/add-ecosystem-doc-evals/tasks.md.\n7. Follow-up evallerina-el4 filed in beads (tokens don't distinguish tools sharing a repo: ah/espectacular); duplicate evallerina-t4g closed; no .beads DB staged in any commit.\n\nVerify against reality:\n- Brief: .wai/projects/evallerina/briefs/evallerina-e4x.md — check claims against it (exact files, red/green mapping, anti-goals pinned).\n- git log: commits 7e3a880..e6c8deb exist and match claimed scope; no .beads in commits.\n- Run gates FRESH: cargo test, just tier0, and the dry-run evidence regeneration (cargo run -- doc-audit plus the propose path) — paste verbatim tails.\n- Confirm no filing occurred (bd list unchanged for other repos; dry-run only).\n- Anti-goals: dry-run default pinned by test; dedup pinned; upstream never filed.\n\nEvidence contract: your final message MUST end with exactly one line: VERDICT: CONFIRM or VERDICT: REVIEW_REQUIRED — citing artifact paths read + fresh command output first."}],"timestamp":1792530152247},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"dB39Vceyv","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"git log --oneline 7e3a880..e6c8deb","timeout":null}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct","usage":{"input":11672,"output":33,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":11705,"cost":{"input":0.0008753999999999999,"output":0.0000066,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.000882}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792530152258,"responseId":"gen-1792530152-ZQcHvWCgckRn95yXaVfB","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"dB39Vceyv","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"e6c8deb style: cargo fmt for e4x routing tests + wai session state (evallerina-e4x)\n3276d92 chore(e4x): task 3.2 dry-run evidence + openspec tasks 3.1–3.2 checked (evallerina-e4x)\n900ad3c chore(beads): close duplicate issue evallerina-t4g (evallerina-e4x)\n3890de4 chore(beads): tracked export after e4x follow-up issue (evallerina-e4x)\nd42b5d9 feat(cli): doc-audit routes audit rows through the filing path, dry-run by default (evallerina-e4x)\n97f0abc test(routing): pin fingerprint-token dedup — same token twice collapses to one proposal (evallerina-e4x)\n4455a6b feat(routing): upstream tools emit skipped/unmapped_upstream, never filed (evallerina-e4x)\n7aa2743 feat(routing): route ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE audit rows through propose() (evallerina-e4x)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792530168959},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"afddbzNef","name":"read","arguments":{"path":".wai/projects/evallerina/briefs/evallerina-e4x.md","offset":1,"limit":200}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct","usage":{"input":11975,"output":41,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":12016,"cost":{"input":0.0008981249999999999,"output":0.000008200000000000001,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0009063249999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792530168961,"responseId":"gen-1792530168-bk6M894ydBsNinINUoT7","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"afddbzNef","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Brief: evallerina-e4x — route audit faults through the filing path\n\nTicket: evallerina-e4x (P2, complexity:m, lane:afk). Feed doc-audit\n`ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED` / `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE` rows through the existing\nfault routing (add-fault-ticket-routing machinery in `src/routing.rs`), per\nopenspec change `add-ecosystem-doc-evals` (tasks 3.1–3.2, design D3/no-new-\nrouting-semantics).\n\n## Why\nSmall surface but high blast radius: it touches the filing path that can\ncreate real tickets in real repos. Delegation with a hard TDD shape keeps\nthe lead lean while forcing the anti-goal tests (no filing without `--file`,\nfingerprint dedup) to be pinned by failing tests first.\n\n## Desired outcome\n1. `src/doc_audit.rs` audit rows are accepted as fault rows by the routing\n   layer: a row with code `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED` or\n   `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE` routes like any other `ERR_*` agent-fault row —\n   fingerprint token `evallerina:<scenario>:<fault-class>`, cross-model\n   threshold `min(3, |registry|)` (existing propose() semantics reused\n   verbatim — no new routing semantics per D3).\n2. Tools with `upstream = true` in routing.toml (`bd`, `openspec`) emit\n   `skipped`/`unmapped_upstream` proposal rows — never filed.\n3. Dry-run by default: `evallerina doc-audit --dry-run` (or the existing\n   propose output path) prints proposal JSONL; filing happens ONLY behind\n   the existing `--file` flag; CI never passes `--file` (anti-goal pinned).\n4. Fingerprint dedup not bypassable: duplicate tokens across runs collapse\n   (existing dedup reused; a test proves double-proposing the same token\n   yields one proposal).\n5. Tasks 3.1: failing test — audit row crosses threshold → dry-run proposal\n   with the fingerprint token. Task 3.2: dry-run smoke against the latest\n   real doc-audit rows (`cargo run -- doc-audit` output) — proposals\n   reviewed and committed as evidence, no filing.\n\n## Exact files\n- `src/routing.rs` — accept doc-audit rows (likely: map audit rows into\n  fault-row shape feeding existing `propose()`; minimal diff)\n- `src/doc_audit.rs` — only if a row-shape bridge function is needed there\n- `src/main.rs` — CLI wiring: doc-audit dry-run proposal output path\n- `tests/routing.rs` — failing tests first (threshold, upstream skip, dedup)\n- NO changes to `report.rs` contract beyond what fok already landed\n\n## Red/green sequence\n1. RED: audit row with `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED` over threshold →\n   `propose()` yields proposal with token\n   `evallerina:<scenario>:ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED`. GREEN.\n2. RED: same for `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`. GREEN.\n3. RED: upstream=true tool's audit row → proposal kind\n   `skipped`/`unmapped_upstream`, never a filing candidate. GREEN.\n4. RED: dedup — same fingerprint token twice → one proposal. GREEN.\n5. Wire CLI dry-run; run task-3.2 smoke against real rows; commit the\n   proposal review as research (no filing).\n\n## Out of scope\n- No actual `bd create` filing in this ticket (73q owns validation)\n- No new check-codes, no report_version changes\n- No scenario/recording work (vrr/t7n)\n\n## Anti-goals\n- No filing without `--file` — pinned by test (CLI test: dry-run default)\n- Fingerprint dedup must not be bypassed — pinned by test\n- upstream=true tools are NEVER filed — pinned by test\n- No new fingerprint token format (reuse existing machinery verbatim)\n\n## Completion criteria\n- `cargo test` exit 0\n- `just tier0` exit 0\n- `cargo run -- doc-audit` + dry-run proposal path → exit 0 with proposals\n  JSONL written to `.wai/projects/evallerina/research/` as task-3.2 evidence\n- openspec tasks 3.1–3.2 checked off\n\n## Follow-up threshold\nIf the existing propose()/dedup machinery resists accepting audit rows\nwithout semantic changes (>1h), STOP and record the impedance as research —\ndo NOT fork a second routing path.\n\n## Verifier evidence contract\nThe verify session's review artifact MUST cite the artifacts it read and\ninclude fresh test-run output (actual commands + verbatim tails) before\nrecording CONFIRM — otherwise REVIEW_REQUIRED.\n\n## Spawn model\nImplementor: `openrouter/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash` (matches PI_PROVIDER default);\ncontext ceiling ≤ 50% of its window, computed at spawn.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792530172155},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"V8jwcLXxw","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cargo test","timeout":null}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"FD4tsuLFr","name":"bash","arguments":{"c